    "body": "## \ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f Description\n\n### What\n1. **Deterministic Semantic Invariant Verification Engine**:\n   - Implemented `verify_semantic_invariant` and `filter_and_ground_semantic_invariants` in `src/webhook_agent/review/grounding.py`.\n   - Purges claims citing non-existent files or phantom repo paths (`_file_exists_in_repo`).\n   - Purges claims asserting nonexistent test definitions (`_test_exists_in_suite`).\n   - Purges citations of phantom domain symbols (`_symbol_exists_in_codebase`).\n   - Demotes residual uncertainty or speculative claims containing hedge language to `unverified_claims`.\n   - Wired verification into `review_enforcer.py` across all review submission paths.\n2. **Elevated Code Auditing Thinking Budget**:\n   - Increased default thinking budget for the code auditor agent to 4096 tokens (from 1024) across `agent_definition.py` and `policy.py`.\n3. **Mandatory Deep Tool Exploration & Anti-One-Shotting Directives**:\n   - Updated `SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION` and `build_transient_turn_content` in `src/webhook_agent/core/prompts.py` to mandate multi-turn tool investigation (`search_files`, `read_file`) before generating a review verdict, explicitly prohibiting premature one-shotting on non-trivial code changes.\n4. **Remediation Documentation**:\n   - Updated `docs/plans/repo_reclamation.md` \u00a77 to formalize the multi-stage deterministic fact-checking architecture.\n\n### Why\n- The code auditor was previously prone to one-shotting PRs without utilizing inspection tools, and occasionally hallucinatory assertions were included in `semantic_invariants` (such as citing non-existent files or fabricated tests).\n- Raising the thinking budget to 4096 gives Gemini 2.5 Flash sufficient reasoning capacity to trace complex cross-file invariant interactions.\n\n### How\n- Path verification validates referenced paths against `git ls-files`.\n- Symbol verification parses repository Python files via AST and inspects declared classes, functions, and methods.\n- Test definition verification inspects test files for actual `def test_...` functions.\n- Triage categorizes speculative claims into `unverified_claims` while preserving grounded guarantees.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddea Testing\n\n### Test Commands\n```bash\n./scripts/ruff-all.sh\nuv run pytest tests/unit/review/test_grounding.py\nuv run pytest tests/unit/review/test_scorecard_floor.py\nuv run pytest --tb=short -q\n```\n\n### Test Results\n- `./scripts/ruff-all.sh`: Ruff check, format check, and MyPy pass 100% cleanly.\n- `tests/unit/review/test_grounding.py`: Added 6 unit tests covering phantom path rejection, phantom symbol rejection, phantom test definition rejection, uncertainty triage, and valid claim preservation.\n- Full suite (`uv run pytest --tb=short -q`): 876 passed, 1 skipped, 36 deselected, 0 failed.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Configuration Impact\n\n- [x] Supports `AUDITOR_THINKING_BUDGET` env override (defaulting to 4096).\n- [x] No changes to `pyproject.toml` dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd12 Security Checklist\n\n- [x] No secrets or credentials hardcoded.\n- [x] HMAC signature verification logic unchanged.\n- [x] Authentication/authorization behavior preserved.\n- [x] Webhook payload handling validated.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Related\n\n- References repo reclamation plan \u00a77.\n",
